       .. versionadded:: 7.1
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option describes the
+   type represented by the alias and is displayed after the name with an equals
+   sign. Its expression is parsed as a Python annotation, so referenced types
+   are cross-referenced. The directive supports a description body and may be
+   nested inside a class.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: Python type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias. This option is optional.
+      When supplied, the expression appears in the signature after the alias
+      name.
+
+   The directive supports the shared Python object options, including
+   ``module`` and ``no-index``.
+
 
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:data:: name
 
